# Master Architecture Plan: The Autonomous Closed-Loop Reasoning "Beast" Engine

## 1. Problem Statement & Core Architectural Diagnosis

The previous agent failed because it was **not an autonomous agent** — it was a **static, open-loop macro player**:
1. It broke user commands into an upfront static array of 4 steps using regex heuristics (`decomposeSingleStage`).
2. It executed those steps blindly via `runStepQueue`.
3. **The LLM was never consulted during execution.**
4. **The Vision Model (`moondream`) was completely shut off** (`vision = ""` in `config.py`).
5. **There was zero sensory feedback**:
   - When GitHub showed `⚠️ siddu already exists in this account`, the agent never read it.
   - When `Create repository` was disabled, JavaScript `.click()` didn't throw an error, so the agent assumed success.
   - When modern Primer dropdowns (`[ Public ▾ ]`) replaced radio buttons, the static script failed silently.

To execute **arbitrary, complex, real-world tasks (even 100 steps)** on ANY website (GitHub, Gmail, Amazon, YouTube, LeetCode, Canva, Wikipedia, internal portals), the agent must operate as a **Closed-Loop Markov Decision Process / ReAct Agent**.

