## 2. The Core Architecture: Closed-Loop ReAct Engine

Every single action in the task lifecycle is governed by the **Perceive $\rightarrow$ Reason $\rightarrow$ Act $\rightarrow$ Verify** loop:

```
                               ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
                               │                     USER COMMAND                       │
                               │  "Create a private repo called siddu with a readme"   │
                               │  "Find the top 3 papers on arXiv and download them"    │
                               │  "Order groceries from cart on Amazon"                │
                               └───────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┘
                                                           │
                                                           ▼
┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                 AUTONOMOUS AGENT REASONING LOOP (Up to 100 Turns)                                     │
│                                                                                                                       │
│  [PHASE 1: LIVE MULTI-MODAL PERCEPTION (Observe)]                                                                     │
│   ├── 1. DOM Semantic Crawler: Extracts all interactive elements (tags, roles, text, values, disabled state).        │
│   ├── 2. Error & Alert Scanner: Scans for active errors ([role="alert"], .flash-error, validation warnings).         │
│   ├── 3. Screen Capture + Privacy Filter: HTML5 canvas masks passwords, Aadhaar, PAN, and sensitive PII.             │
│   └── 4. Moondream VLM Comprehension: Fast visual scan for open dialogs, modal backdrops, popups, and banners.        │
│                                                                                                                       │
│  [PHASE 2: DEEP REASONING & DECISION (Qwen2.5-3B)]                                                                    │
│   ├── Ingests: Goal + Current URL + Screen Context + Live Error Alerts + Interactive Elements + Action History.       │
│   ├── Thinks:                                                                                                         │
│   │   • What was the outcome of my last action? Did an error appear?                                                  │
│   │   • Is the target button disabled? If yes, what prerequisite is missing?                                          │
│   │   • Is there an obscuring popup/modal that must be dismissed first?                                               │
│   │   • What is the single best next action to move closer to the goal?                                               │
│   └── Outputs Structured JSON:                                                                                        │
│       {                                                                                                               │
│         "thought": "I notice that 'siddu' is already taken. The submit button is disabled. I will change it to ...",  │
│         "action": { "type": "type", "tag_id": 2, "value": "siddu-dev" },                                              │
│         "is_done": false                                                                                              │
│       }                                                                                                               │
│                                                                                                                       │
│  [PHASE 3: GROUNDED ROBUST EXECUTION (content.js)]                                                                    │
│   ├── 1. Pre-Condition Guard: Throws error if attempting to click disabled elements (prevents false completions).    │
│   ├── 2. Modern Control Dispatch: Handles ActionMenus, Primer dropdowns, Popovers, switches, contenteditable.        │
│   ├── 3. Native Event Synthesis: PointerEvent + MouseEvent + React _valueTracker reset + input/change dispatch.       │
│   └── 4. Mutation Quiescence: Waits for DOM mutations to settle (150ms debounce) so SPAs fully hydrate.              │
│                                                                                                                       │
│  [PHASE 4: STATE VERIFICATION & LOOP CONTINUATION]                                                                    │
│   ├── If is_done == true: Verify real post-condition (e.g. URL changed or success confirmation exists).               │
│   ├── If action caused navigation: Background worker intercepts chrome.tabs.onUpdated and resumes loop.               │
│   └── Record (Turn, Thought, Action, Result) into sliding-window History -> Proceed to Turn t+1.                      │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

